{"Title":"An Act relative to the collateral consequences of alimony","BillNumber":"S969","DocketNumber":"SD1139","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"PRF0","Name":"Paul R. Feeney","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PRF0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T16:48:39.66"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"PRF0","Name":"Paul R. Feeney","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PRF0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T16:48:39.66"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S969/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Feeney, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 969) of Paul R. Feeney for legislation relative to the federal tax collateral consequences of alimony.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSection 53 of chapter 208 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2016 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after the word “incomes”, in line 14, the following words:- \", if federally tax deductible, or, if not federally tax deductible, the recipient’s need or 23 per cent to 28 per cent of the difference between the parties’ gross incomes, as\".\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}